## S02-001 baseline - 2026-07-18

`S02-001` establishes the first bounded registry baseline:

* Canonical conductor manifest, binding, capability, permission, witness, typed I/O, and runtime-profile types resolve to `omega_contracts`.
* `omega_state` imports those types and owns bounded execution, independent reconstruction, replay, and terminal receipts.
* One deterministic fixture gauge and one canned Codex model-profile fixture replay preserve the same semantic output, permissions, write surface, evidence ceiling, witness set, and literal `AuthorityEffect::None`.
* Missing capabilities route to survivor `OperatorNeeded` under terminal `OpenObstruction`; expansion requires `LiftLicenseNeeded`; an unavailable adapter routes to `InfrastructureFailure`.
* The frozen packet, observer, source manifest, identities, budgets, exact writes, hostile matrix, and no-network/no-credential boundary are machine-checked.

This baseline is not provider activation or general gauge interchangeability. SAGA-02 remains `ACTIVE` because `S02-002` must separately implement and review GTOC-3 lift-trigger and license completeness. No gate is enabled by this lifecycle transition.
